<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17129" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">expugnātor</span></b> ,
		ōris, m.
		expugno, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the taker</i>, <i>stormer</i>, <i>conqueror</i> of a place. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop. (rare but class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Inv. 1, 50, 93</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Prov. 16, 32</span></i>
			: rex Demetrius Expugnator cognominatus (transl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πολιορκητής</span>), <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 38,
				39, § 126</span></i>.— * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pecoris opimi lupus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 4, 363</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pudicitiae,</span>”
				<i>a violator</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 1, 4, § 9</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
